  "body": "According to the spec, the state of the image request for an image element is initially unavailable [1]. When a user agent is required to check the usability of the image argument, where image is a HTMLOrSVGImageElement object for which the source is not set, the state of the image request remains unavailable. In this case, the user agent must return \"bad\" without raising en exception [2].\r\nThe spec already covers this situation, but a clarification seems to help as this was misinterpreted in a web platform test (now fixed).\r\n\r\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#images-processing-model\r\n[2] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#image-sources-for-2d-rendering-contexts\r\n\r\n",
